#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515514 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186515297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515514 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fdada9a0-319d-50fa-a0c4-8211688157c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515518 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515518 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515518 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515518 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x,$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\cdot g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515518 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "05fabaa5-d0f1-544a-aecb-26138b15f8e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515518 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{csch}⁡4x+{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{csch}⁡4x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\cdot {{(1-2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x)}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=1-2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515540 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515540 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95569" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515540 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515540 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515540 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "51513d5e-ca42-5754-a902-1af12bc25041" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515540 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡g,\\,g={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515545 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515545 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95450" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515545 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515545 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515545 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58b4a157-5f9c-5f77-a21d-1b131c8f0140" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515545 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =4(-{csch}^{2}⁡x)-(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{csch}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515547 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515547 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95585" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515547 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515547 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515547 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "598d9b4b-1def-5b7e-8724-7abe41dc985d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515547 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=2{x}^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2{x}^{3}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2{x}^{3}\\cdot (-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-2{x}^{3}{csch}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515553 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515553 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95568" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515553 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515553 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=4\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515553 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6703e5b6-66a0-5cda-938a-ed7160c9206e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515553 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=4\\operatorname{sech}⁡g,\\,g=3x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=-4\\operatorname{sech}⁡g\\operatorname{tanh}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-4\\operatorname{sech}⁡g\\operatorname{tanh}⁡g\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sech}⁡g\\operatorname{tanh}⁡g \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515555 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515555 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95566" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515555 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515555 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515555 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6866b59d-bbba-56df-8e9c-26cc543fc023" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515555 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g,\\,g=1-4x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1-4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515559 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515559 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95893" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515559 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515559 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{g(x)}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$ What is $g(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515559 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6cac54f6-b1ee-5704-8eb2-39e7e0d78de0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515559 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\overset{g(x)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)}}}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515561 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515561 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515561 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515561 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡({x}^{2}-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76beb3b0-dbd8-5192-b70b-0a4bac401337" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515561 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\\,g={x}^{2}-1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=-{csch}^{2}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-{csch}^{2}⁡g\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-2x{csch}^{2}⁡g \\\\  & =-2x{csch}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515565 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515565 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95581" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515565 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515565 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515565 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b044358-869c-54b8-ba0e-868b6f91f848" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515565 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=2x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot (-2x{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515569 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515569 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95892" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515569 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515569 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{g(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}.$ What is $g(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515569 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8386701e-f444-5c82-8928-9b7b2e5dd7d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515569 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\overset{g(x)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515575 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515575 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95889" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515575 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515575 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515575 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9031fff8-a36e-5cc9-9588-e90f1f428aa9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515575 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-{x}^{2}(-2\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515590 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95478" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515590 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515590 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515590 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b84615c0-35fb-546b-b311-f278e0c613e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515590 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515591 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515591 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95577" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515591 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515591 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2{sech}^{2}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515591 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b9b1e144-f837-55bf-a0c3-8113231511af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515591 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=2{g}^{2},\\,g=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4g(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515601 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515601 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95588" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515601 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515601 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-3x{csch}^{2}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515601 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ca80da50-025a-555f-9c99-42892fcfd87d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515601 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=-3x$ and $v(x)={csch}^{2}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-3x)}^{′}\\cdot {csch}^{2}⁡x+(-3x)\\cdot {({csch}^{2}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {csch}^{2}⁡x-3x\\cdot (2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3{csch}^{2}⁡x+6x{csch}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\  & =3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515605 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515605 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95896" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515605 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515605 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{{3}^{x}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515605 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d2bf0ce7-0ebf-56f9-bf0e-f167e2403753" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515605 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)={3}^{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot {3}^{x}-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {({3}^{x})}^{′}}{{({3}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)\\cdot {3}^{x}-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot ({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{3}^{x}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515609 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515609 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515609 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515609 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=6\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515609 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0bc8c85-75bd-5d02-9581-c62ed55b672c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515609 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =6(-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6{csch}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
